    <string name="help_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="help_1">Your players run on their own. You only decide when to let go of the ball.</string>
    <string name="help_2">When one of your players has the ball it circles around them, and an arrow shows where it would go. Touch and hold anywhere to keep it; lift your finger to send it.</string>
    <string name="help_3">The arrow turns green when it points at a team-mate (a pass) and pink when it points at the goal (a shot). Releasing near a target snaps to it, so you don\'t need to be exact. The ball spins towards the most useful target first.</string>
    <string name="help_4">Defenders who reach your carrier steal the ball. Keep it moving: pass, pass, shoot.</string>
    <string name="help_5">Start with Training: the first drills have no opponents, then dummies, then defenders that get faster each level.</string>
    <string name="help_6">The season has a league and a cup, played in five worlds. Your team\'s automatic play follows the tactics on the coach\'s board.</string>
